<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="035" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>Legal Front Door intake submit endpoint (FR-05 server, FR-06 intake half)</title>
    <phase>3 BFF features</phase>
    <gate>after 011, 020 and 033</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New external write endpoint (tags bff-api, auth)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>New write path gated by plane switch and Tier-1 entitlement</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>endpoint-registration chain in ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs: 033 → 035 → 037</parallel-reason>
    <deps>011, 020, 033</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add POST /api/v1/external/servicerequests that creates a sprk_servicerequest from a Legal Front Door wizard submission, for workforce callers always and for CIAM callers only when the partner switch is on.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. ASP.NET Core and Dataverse developer. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>The submit route validates the request type and answers, requires the legal-front-door module entitlement, creates one sprk_servicerequest app-only with sprk_requestedby = the caller's contact, sprk_requesttype, sprk_intakedata, sprk_name and sprk_direction = Inbound, and returns its id; the row then appears in the caller's Service Requests tab.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>C2: four wizards (NDA Assessment, Invention Submission, Policy Question, Trademark Search) write sprk_servicerequest. No intake endpoint exists (grep 2026-10-10). Task 020 adds sprk_requesttype and sprk_intakedata. sprk_name and sprk_direction are required (live describe). The Service Requests module lists rows by sprk_requestedby (ExternalAccessModule.cs:444-455); task 011 adds the partner switch and the CIAM legal-front-door default.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalIntakeEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalDataService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ModuleEntitlementResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="new-artifact">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalIntakeEndpointsTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Every route this task adds or modifies is mapped inside the /api/v1/external group (Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:60-63) so it inherits the ExternalCollaboration policy and CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter. No route in this task is mapped outside that group.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">No OBO on the external plane: every Dataverse and SPE call this task adds is app-only and scoped to the caller's accessible set (spec NFR-01).</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">State the Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md). Measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build: more than +5 MB needs written justification; the total must stay at or under 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Build only on the net10 SDK (10.0.1xx). Run /conflict-check before opening the PR: Api/ExternalAccess/** and Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** are shared with unified-access-control-r2.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A3">The route is denied server-side (403) when the caller is not entitled to the legal-front-door module; it never relies on the client hiding the card.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">CIAM callers are refused (403) unless ExternalAccess:PartnerServiceRequestsEnabled is true.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">sprk_requestedby is the caller's contact from the resolved principal; a caller with no contact gets 403 with a clear reason. Request fields that name a requester, owner or creator are ignored.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">sprk_intakedata stores the validated answers as JSON (max 100 KB); unknown request types return 400.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>service request intake</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/spec.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-001-minimal-api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/oauth-scopes.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/auth-deployment-setup.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/data-model/sprk_servicerequest.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files listed above, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Read the module entitlement check used by existing gated routes and the service-requests descriptor.</step>
    <step order="2">Create ExternalIntakeEndpoints.cs (Map method called from ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs in the external group) with POST /servicerequests.</step>
    <step order="3">Validate: requestType ∈ the four values; title required (→ sprk_name); answers JSON object ≤ 100 KB.</step>
    <step order="4">Create the row app-only via ExternalDataService with requestedby, requesttype, intakedata, name, direction = Inbound.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: workforce caller → 201 and the row is in the caller's service-requests set; CIAM caller with switch off → 403; with switch on → 201 and visible only to that caller; unentitled caller → 403; unknown type → 400; oversize answers → 400; body naming another requester → ignored.</step>
    <step order="6">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` (0 errors) and `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` (all pass); measure publish size per .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md and record it in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations, decisions and measurements in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/notes/task-035-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a licensed workforce systemuser caller has no contact (so sprk_requestedby cannot be set), STOP and escalate — it decides whether licensed staff can submit.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No intake/service-request submit endpoint exists in Api/ExternalAccess (grep 2026-10-10); R2 task 031 (typed-intake framework) was never built.</existing>
    <extension>No: there is no service-request write path to extend; the row create reuses ExternalDataService and the stamping/entitlement seams.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The four quick-start wizards cannot create a request (R2 UAT 4B; spec FR-05).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalIntakeEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalIntakeEndpointsTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A workforce caller submitting a valid NDA Assessment gets 201 and a sprk_servicerequest with requesttype NDA Assessment, the answers in sprk_intakedata, requestedby = the caller's contact and direction Inbound.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">That row is returned by the caller's Service Requests module read and by no other caller's.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A CIAM caller gets 403 while the partner switch is off.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With the switch on, a CIAM caller's submission succeeds and is visible only to that caller.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A caller not entitled to legal-front-door gets 403.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An unknown request type or answers over 100 KB return 400.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A requester named in the body is ignored.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build is green; all unit tests pass; publish size is recorded and at or under 60 MB with no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative and edge cases named in these criteria. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-05, FR-06. Client wizards: tasks 052, 053.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting this task, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow the task-execute skill for the mandatory pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
